Hey, I'm working on an embedded C++ project for an automotive ECU and I've run into a serious issue. The system has a gradual RAM exhaustion that only shows up after about 4-5 hours of continuous operation. It's not a massive spike, just a slow crawl until we hit a hard fault. 

Here is a snippet of the main telemetry loop where I suspect the issue might be occurring, though I can't find any obvious missing deletes:

```cpp
void process_sensor_data(SensorData* data) {
    if (data != nullptr) {
        LogEntry* entry = new LogEntry(data->timestamp, data->value);
        buffer.push_back(entry);

        if (buffer.size() > MAX_BUFFER_SIZE) {
            // Logic to rotate logs
            for (size_t i = 0; i < buffer.size() - MAX_BUFFER_SIZE; ++i) {
                // We need to clean up old entries here
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Can you give me a systematic approach to identifying where this leak is coming from? Standard valgrind isn't an option on this hardware.

